==== markdown
# core/hello

The smallest module a repository can hold

## Where it is built

minimal

## What it exchanges

Nothing: it neither provides nor requires.

## What it declares to install

| Family | Packages | Enabled repository |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `fedora` | `fastfetch` | `updates-testing` |
| `fedora` | `example-tool` | `copr:copr.fedorainfracloud.org:example:tools` |

| Family | Groups | Enabled repository |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `fedora` | `core` | default |

## What it claims

Nothing. It declares no `satisfies`.

## Where it came from

| Content | Hash |
| --- | --- |
| declared | `33877acc20d198115512d34f23bc7481d0cd20ff656dc49e6931a2aa7986e318` |

It was written in this repository rather than imported, so nothing upstream to compare it against.

## What it pulls in

Nothing. It declares no `asset`.

## Third-party repositories

It enables these COPR repositories, each disabled again so it is on for the install and not in the shipped image.

| COPR | URL |
| --- | --- |
| example/tools | https://copr.fedorainfracloud.org/coprs/example/tools/ |

It enables one, in `modules/core/hello/repo`. There is no grammar for that file, so read it: it is shell calling the family's config manager.

| URL it names |
| --- |
| https://example.invalid/updates-testing.repo |

